WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
In this video, you will add photos to an event you posted, and learn where to find your events.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:06.660
We start on the map.

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:09.633
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.340
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.160
Then tap Allow.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.000
Look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.760
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:26.660
Tap it.

00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:30.354
In the menu, tap Your events.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.600
It opens the events you added.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.340
Here is your event.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.020
It says whether it is on the map, and it shows the buttons for it.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.420
Tap Edit.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.900
Find the Photos box.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.960
You can add up to four photos.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.640
Photos are saved right away, so you do not need to tap Save.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.040
Tap Add photos, and choose pictures from your phone or computer.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.260
The first photo is the cover.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.960
It is the picture on the map list and at the top of your event page.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.700
To use a different one, tap Cover on it.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.660
To take a photo off, tap the x on it.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.820
Your photos show first on the map and on the event page, credited to the organizer.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.440
If you remove them all, the picture from your event's web page comes back.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.880
Just below the photos is an optional Video link.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.420
Paste a YouTube or Vimeo link there.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:24.720
Then tap Save.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.260
Your event now has a Watch the video button.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.180
The video loads only when someone taps it.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.100
Now back to Your events.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:43.160
If your event is cancelled or postponed, choose that in the notice menu on the event, so visitors do not drive out for nothing.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.680
You can clear it later.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.800
That is how you manage an event you posted.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.920
Your photos and video show on the map and on the event page.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.900
Next up: Show off your home.

